+    <h2>1. Privacy by Design &amp; Data Minimization</h2>
+    <p>
+        The DevTools Times is built on the principle of <strong>data minimization</strong>: if we do not collect personal data, we cannot lose or misuse it. You can browse all articles, reports, and multimedia and maintain a session-based reading list as a guest without creating an account.
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Minimal Account Data:</strong> If you choose to create an account, we only ask for a username (which can be a pseudonym) and a password. We never ask for your legal name, email address, phone number, exact date of birth, or physical address.</li>
+        <li><strong>Purpose Limitation:</strong> Credentials provided on our <a href={`${baseUrl}signin`}>Sign In</a> and <a href={`${baseUrl}signup`}>Sign Up</a> forms are used strictly for account authentication and never repurposed for marketing, profiling, or advertising.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>2. Third-Party Scripts &amp; Subresources</h2>
+    <p>
+        We do not load third-party click-tracking analytics scripts or invasive advertising SDKs in our page layout. External font stylesheets are loaded with anonymous CORS mode (<code>crossorigin="anonymous"</code>) and <code>referrerpolicy="no-referrer"</code> so your browsing path is not leaked to font CDNs.
+    </p>
+
+    <h2>3. Cookies, Local Storage &amp; Document Security Headers</h2>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>No Sensitive Data in Web Storage:</strong> We never store authentication tokens or personally identifiable information (PII) in <code>localStorage</code> or <code>sessionStorage</code>.</li>
+        <li><strong>First-Party Session State:</strong> Your bookmarked reading list is stored in an encrypted, server-managed session cookie rather than third-party tracking cookies.</li>
+        <li><strong>Privacy-Preserving HTTP Headers:</strong> Every document response enforces <code>Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code>, a restrictive <code>Permissions-Policy</code> disabling camera, microphone, geolocation, and motion sensors by default, and strict framing and resource isolation headers.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>4. Your Data Rights, Erasure &amp; Control</h2>
+    <p>
+        Opting out, clearing your browser state, or deleting your account is as effortless as signing up. At any time on the <a href={`${baseUrl}signin`}>Sign In</a> or <a href={`${baseUrl}signup`}>Sign Up</a> page, you can use the <strong>Sign Out &amp; Clear Site Data</strong> or <strong>Delete Account &amp; Erase Data</strong> controls, which send the HTTP <code>Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"</code> header to immediately purge all site cookies, storage, and cached data from your browser.
+    </p>
